  "conditions": "6 AM—Up and at 'em! The early mountain birds will certainly be catching the worms. Springtime seems determined to make a premature debut, so just go with the flow and take in the panoramic view. Fast-softening snow will provide forgiving sliding surfaces as high temperatures zoar well into the 40s at the summit and approach an outlandish 70 in Teton Village. A slight reprieve from the solar radiation will come from gusty west winds in the 10 to 30 mph range. Winter isn't over yet, so don't sit around getting bored and lazy. It's going to be OK. Let this epic heatwave melt your rational mind because you just may find that skiing is much better when you go a little crazy. -Lege",
